            <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.qjq2bvqc2>,
            <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.sj3tx9648> ;
        mlt:candidateDatasetTitle "Data from: Effect of composition on shape of bird eggs",
            "Data from: Pelvis morphology suggests that early Mesozoic birds were too heavy to contact incubate their eggs",
            "Data from: The evolution of egg shape in birds: Evolutionary constraints and adaptations",
            "To hop or not to hop? the answer is in the bird trees" ;
        mlt:citation "Thompson, D.W. (1917) On Growth and Form. Cambridge University Press. Ch. XVII, pp. 757-759, Figs. 388-393." ;
        mlt:claim "The pelves of Archaeopteryx and Apatornis (after Heilmann) and intermediate configurations can be found by interpolation between coordinate-transformed forms - i.e. interpolated grids generate biologically real intermediate forms." ;
        mlt:claimId "T1917-054" ;
        mlt:counterclaim "Heilmann's interpolation idea became standard machinery (TPS interpolation between landmark configurations is exactly how morphometricians now generate intermediates), so the *method* was vindicated by adoption. The *biological* claim -- that grid-interpolated forms are the real intermediate forms -- is only testable against fossils, and the literature does not test it on Heilmann's bird pelves." ;
        mlt:dataKindNeeded "bird pelvis landmarks (literature assembly)" ;
        mlt:datasetAuditReason "Dryad live search returned 4 title-relevant dataset(s), top: doi:10.5061/dryad.k1v34cf." ;
        mlt:datasetExistence "PUBLIC_SCRIPTABLE" ;
        mlt:dateMade "1917"^^xsd:gYear ;
        mlt:effortDaysHigh 20 ;
        mlt:effortDaysLow 10 ;
        mlt:instantiatesWorkflow <https://w3id.org/morpholib/thompson/process/1917-claim-validation-workflow> ;
        mlt:literatureArtifact <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/thompson_1917_counterclaims.json> ;
        mlt:literatureCitation "Bookstein (1989) IEEE TPAMI 11:567-585; Rohlf's tps software literature (from 1990)" ;
        mlt:literatureRelation "QUALIFIED" ;
        mlt:literatureWhoAndWhen "Bookstein (1989) and the TPS/ancestral-reconstruction literature" ;
        mlt:pass2Status "PARTIAL_REPO" ;
        mlt:step5Status "PENDING Step 5: Steps 1-4 completed (dataset PUBLIC_SCRIPTABLE, tier LOOP_WITH_SEED); loop slot queued in thompson/thompson_1917_loop_queue.yaml." ;
